5857:  // writer of a description is Tickets___update_ticket, which the orchestrator
      -> the single hit is the explanatory COMMENT at 5857 and a remark at 1758.
         No call. Tickets___update_ticket is an AGENT-facing tool; the rewrite is an
         orchestrator-side prompt transformation. The two never meet.

--- 5. Scope caveats on the rewrite that DOES happen ---
  * CONSUMERS ONLY: the guard is `TICKET_PLAN_VALIDATOR !== "off" && branchPlan &&
    !branchPlan.producer` (5868). A producer persona's prompt is byte-identical in
    every mode — so the sweeper ticket TEAM-4230 itself, the ticket the acceptance
    text names, is exactly the one whose prose is NOT rewritten. Its downstream
    reviewer/QA/CI consumers are the ones that see the corrected name.
  * MODE SPLIT: shadow computes the rewrite and publishes
    ticket_plan.branch_rewritten_observed, but line 5892 gates the substitution on
    `=== "enforce"`, so only enforce changes the prompt bytes.

--- CONCLUSION (stated plainly, as requested) ---
  Under TICKET_PLAN_VALIDATOR=enforce the invented branch name
  `chore/dead-code-sweep-2026-09-07` IS replaced by `feature/TEAM-4230-code-sweeper`
  in the DISPATCH CONTEXT of consumer personas, and an event records it. NOTHING
  writes that correction back to the Jira issue or the DynamoDB ticket row, so
  anyone reading the ticket in Jira/the UI still sees the invented branch. The
  acceptance sentence "is rewritten ... IN THE TICKET BODY" is therefore FALSE as
  written; the implemented behaviour is context-only, which is what the dev notes say.
